From: openEuler package maintenance
Subject: [PATCH] bfcalc: reject invalid file lengths and failed file I/O
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Source: https://bellard.org/libbf/libbf-2025-06-03.tar.gz
Source-SHA256: 4b23394d67a4a3c3266a38b66831094523fffb5d01974a5c05a0327b36b0a340
Original-file: bfcalc.c
Original-file-SHA256: b6e805a51cff6058db6479a2411eda76157c8c4013c4183b17e5ebc124b90a2f
Applies-to: official LibBF 2025-06-03 (RPM version 2025.06.03), native bfcalc
Root-cause: unchecked seek/tell/narrowing/allocation/read results reach a buffer write.
Upstream-status: not submitted; no upstream write is authorized.
Remove-when: a later reviewed official source checks equivalent file-I/O and
 length/allocation boundaries and retains empty, regular and nonseekable regressions.
Scope: preserve original fatal load-error convention, parser/caller, defaults,
 original Pi checks, arithmetic APIs and compilation/hardening flags.
Evidence: source-visible error path only; no runtime crash, exploit or CVE claim.

The following complete original bfcalc.c MIT notice is retained for this
source-derived patch; original unmodified member notices remain packaged:
